findings.suggested_fix:
Preferred: a behavioural rewrite. Keep the target: complex Gaussian noise confined to -10..-2 kHz with nothing at positive frequencies, the 90 % / quarter 20-30 % / two < 1 % limits, RMS 0.6 +/- 5 %, 50 kHz with no rate change, the File Sink and type, and 'keep running'. Drop the prescriptive sentence 'Start from ... RMS 1.5 ... cutoffs ... 500 Hz ... unity gain', or recast it as non-binding background, for example 'for reference, white noise of RMS 1.5 through an ideal unity-gain 8 kHz-wide band gives RMS 0.6'. The model then has to choose the source level and the filter itself. Keep a structural phrase such as 'filtered noise' only together with the F2 graph check.
If the team keeps the design wording instead, then:
- add stated, checkable edge/width limits (for example narrow-band power shares just outside the -6 dB points);
- add near-miss mutants (width 1500 Hz; cutoffs moved 250-400 Hz) that the oracle must kill;
- record a team decision that the amp/gain split and the source distribution are accepted as unobservable.
Either way, update P6/P9 in spec_properties.
